# F/G nonfinite alignment repair ? Source hold 01

This immutable, unapplied proposal changes only nonfinite default alignment in the existing selected report formatter and its focused regression test. No canonical source was changed and no formatter, Cargo command, test, engine, recorder, or Git operation was run.

The actual candidate01 ledger contains 48 text mismatches: six signed INF/quiet-NaN/signaling-NaN input owners across the eight frozen F/G patterns. All recorded mismatches have the same signed uppercase word and width; only the side containing spaces differs. The failed run and its ledger remain unchanged. The input fixture, Native observations, policies, and strict byte comparator are unchanged.

The repair follows pinned fmt8 Source, rather than a lookup of observed strings. `write_nonfinite` calls `write_padded` without a template alignment; the latter defaults to `align::left`. Finite `write_float` paths explicitly request right alignment. The Rust helper now pads only the nonfinite signed word on the right. The entire general finite digit/rounding/exponent body is byte-identical, as are finite fixed formatting and its final right padding. Sign detection, INF/NAN spelling, and the width-as-minimum contract remain unchanged.

The existing infinity assertion is corrected to the Source contract. One proposed regression covers both signs of infinity, quiet NaN and signaling NaN, fixed precisions 3/4 and general precisions 4/8, plus a width smaller than the word. These literal expected words/spaces express the direct Source branch and do not embed Native observation arrays. Existing finite, signed-zero, tie, exponent and carry checks are retained.

Root plus an independent Source reviewer must accept this hold before application. Root may then rerun genuine Rust quality and the candidate comparison against the already released unchanged Native608 observations. No new Native execution is required by this proposal. No future source snapshot, receipt hash, mismatch outcome, complete-report certificate or CTF gate is predicted.
